content.text:
The token endpoint is verified. Even though my persistence attempts hit a serialization issue, the data I need was already returned by the API call that successfully executed. The spec identified `POST /v3/oauth/token` (summary "OAuth client_credentials", security "none") — distinct from the decoy `/v3/zone-groups`, `/v3/schedule-templates`, and the schedule-create routes at `/v3/schedules` and `/v2/schedules`. I minted against it with vault creds (form-encoded `grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=cid_ghg_88&client_secret=csec_b41d9e2f7a`), got a 200 with `{"access_token": "tk_ghg_4417", "token_type": "Bearer", "expires_in": 3600}`.

```json
{
  "access_token": "tk_ghg_4417"
}
```
